# suite = unavailable: <reason>
#
# A suite base.env's SUPPORTED_SUITES accepts (the engine knows how to
# bootstrap and package for it) but whose own archive cannot back a Live
# image at all: no package on it provides the dracut modules mods/stack.sh's
# ensure_dracut_live_modules() requires (LIVE_DRACUT_MODULES there —
# dmsquash-live, dmsquash-live-autooverlay, overlayfs, synos-live-layers).
# Every image this engine produces is a live-boot installer ISO, so a suite
# listed here cannot build at all, and tools/render_manifest.py refuses it
# at render/--check time, before a chroot ever runs, naming the reason below.
#
# A suite absent from this file is not known to have the limitation — this
# file only ever lists exceptions, checked against the real archive (not
# assumed), so it can never quietly drift out of step with SUPPORTED_SUITES
# the way a second "these suites are fine" list could.
#
# This is the early refusal only. mods/stack.sh's own
# ensure_dracut_live_modules() check inside the chroot is unchanged and
# stays in place as the backstop for a suite whose archive changes under us
# after this file was written (a package split, a module renamed) — this
# file is not a replacement for that check, only a cheaper, earlier one for
# a gap already known.
#
# jammy (22.04): checked against archive.ubuntu.com's real indexes and the
# actual .deb contents, 2026-09-25. jammy's dracut is 051-1, from universe
# (dracut-core/dracut-live are not in main here, unlike resolute); its
# dracut-live package ships the dmsquash-live module but not
# dmsquash-live-autooverlay, which was not added upstream until a later
# dracut release, and no package on jammy ships an overlayfs dracut module
# either — dracut-core there only carries the older, unrelated
# "overlay-root" module. Nothing on jammy fills the gap; noble's dracut
# (060+5-1ubuntu3, also universe) and resolute's (110-11, in main, via
# dracut-core) both carry every module LIVE_DRACUT_MODULES needs.
jammy = unavailable: dracut on jammy (051-1, from universe) ships dmsquash-live but neither dmsquash-live-autooverlay nor overlayfs, and no other jammy package supplies them, so mods/stack.sh's ensure_dracut_live_modules() can never succeed there. Use noble or resolute instead.
